  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "**a test is a declaration carrying the authored `test` marker and nothing else, but the native lane restated that identity as a LOCATION predicate beside it (the module's namespace had to be v2.test (a namespace prefix) or below, spelled twice: once where the universe was derived and once where the receipt was judged, plus a hand-mirrored copy of the default pattern in the seed, spelled in two seed functions and passed to the emitted compiler on every native run) -- so a marked declaration outside the predicate was silently not a test and a module named inside it was a test candidate whatever it contained (INVALID STATE: two authorities for one fact, `what is a test`, which disagree on every marked declaration outside v2.test (a namespace prefix) and are checked against each other by nothing).**",
    "REPAIR LANDED WITH THIS ROW (source layout authority, audit item 2): the universe is the marked declarations of the acquired modules and the pattern only SELECTS within it by label; the two namespace predicates are deleted; the default pattern is the route boundary `//v2/...` and `native_route_default_pattern` is the only AUTHORED spelling of it (the seed holds a constant rendered from that one declaration, below); a duplicate (module, declaration) marker identity and a marked declaration no label can name refuse the lane; the enumeration of a single named namespace is deleted with its claims. Controls: `v2.test.claim.native_lane_universe_selection` (marked outside v2.test (a namespace prefix), unmarked inside it, duplicate marker identity, a malformed module holding a marker-shaped spelling refused rather than read as zero tests) and `v2.test.v2_native_route` (the boundary, the entries, the nonempty-where-required contract through `an_empty_universe_is_refused`).",
    "THE SEED'S COPY OF THE NATIVE BOUNDARY IS CONSTRUCTED, NOT MIRRORED: the emitted driver defaults to `native_route_default_pattern()` itself (`adjudicate <facts> [--pattern <p>] <roots>...`; an absent flag is the compiler's own default and a dangling flag refuses, with no fallback), so the seed's lane runner and frontier pass NO pattern; and the seed's pre-binary routing (`gunbc test <operand>` decides native-or-claim before any binary exists, so the declaration cannot be evaluated at that point) parses `NATIVE_ROUTE_DEFAULT_PATTERN` from `native_route_seed_boundary_generated.rs`, which `gunbc.native_route_seed_boundary_emit` renders from the one declaration and the generated-artifact registry holds to it. A constant that does not parse is a typed refusal of the verb, not a panic and not a default. Controls: `test.claim.native_route_seed_boundary_witness` (the authority-movement claim: the expected bytes carry the declaration's rendering, a moved pattern carries its own rendering with no trace of the old one, and the moved bytes differ from the default's, which is the exact condition under which a committed file left unregenerated is a located drift finding) and `v2.test.claim.native_driver_plan` (the default, the explicit pattern not replaced by the default, the flag recognised only after the facts path, the dangling flag refused).",
    "RESIDUAL, DISCLOSED, NOT REPAIRED HERE -- the claim route's universe is still a hand mirror: `gunbc.discovery_census` `claim_route_universe` (`//test/claim/...`) is restated in the seed (`target_invocation_host` `claim_route_universe`) with nothing joining the two, so the same fork survives one level out for the OTHER route. It is not projected by this change: the claim route's universe is the discovery census's own declaration, and widening or projecting it is the decision the NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER below already owns.",
    "RESIDUAL, NOT REPAIRED HERE -- the same fork one level out, in the ROUTES rather than the lane: a marked declaration in a module under `dag/test/manual/` is selected by neither route. The native lane's boundary is the `v2` namespace; `gunbc.discovery_census` `claim_route_universe` is the `//test/claim/...` label subtree; and `test/manual/` is a declared `OfflineLocalRecipe` exclusion of the required floor (`gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots`), whose own dissolution is that the manual suites migrate under `test/claim` with declared consumers. A declaration there that carries the marker is therefore a test that no `gunbc test` operand reaches -- a test-loss gap, whose population is re-derivable as the marked declarations of the modules `git ls-files dag/test/manual` lists. It is not closed by one value: the claim route executes the sites discovery enumerates, and discovery excludes `test/manual/` by that declared row, so a `//test/...` operand would admit labels whose population discovery has excluded by declaration -- an operand that selects nothing silently, or a new typed refusal, and in either case a decision on the offline recipes that a widened pattern value does not make. The widening is therefore the capability named below, not a change to the universe value.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- nothing refused the disagreement. The universe was a filter on top of the marker, so the lane answered a smaller question than the marker defines and reported it as the whole, and the receipt clause that should have caught a member outside the universe was the same predicate spelled a second time.",
    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed for the lane (the marker is the only input to identity, so no namespace predicate has a constructor in the universe derivation; the duplicate and unlabelable marker shapes are typed refusals at derivation). RUNG ESTABLISHED, PER PATH: the lane's universe and the compiler's default pattern are at the ceiling; the seed's native-boundary constant is MECHANICALLY PREVENTABLE and no higher, because a committed `native_route_seed_boundary_generated.rs` that disagrees with the declaration remains writable, and what stops it is the generated-artifact drift wall plus heal's regeneration, neither of which is on the required `witnesses` job (the declared drop `v1_required_lanes_withdrawn`, whose trigger is the native compiler judging that population); the claim route's mirror is mitigatable at best, with nothing joining it to its declaration. The route-level residual is decidable and its ceiling is the same once the claim executor's population is defined; it is below ceiling today.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, naming the capability: the claim route enumerates every marked declaration of the modules its operand reaches -- a population defined by the marker through the same acquired-module fold the native lane uses -- sufficient for `gunbc test` over `//test/...` to select, run or refuse each marked declaration of `dag/test/manual/` and to leave every unmarked declaration out, with the offline-recipe exclusion stated as a typed refusal of that selection and not as a missing route.",
